      "message": "\u003e Though there are many signals in power sequence, only one set we are monitoring actively, sleep signals and some power good signals, generated by GPIO/VW interrupts or other source. I refer them as power signals. The implementation that how to monitor those signals using a bitmap to check/wait those signals. Put all signals in one array can use a universal set/get interface, that\u0027s good. Though I really need a enum defined in a consecutive order too for monitoring signals implementation. Also from those enum can get signal value.\n\nSo the enum power_signal should be consecutive order, so you should be able to use them as a bit array. That was the plan. This code should fully support that.\nThe range is 0 through to POWER_SIGNAL_COUNT.\n\nI was scratching my head about how to handle \u0027optional\u0027 signals, where the current code was using DTS node checks.\nI came to the conclusion that this is likely best handled by CONFIG_ items rather than using DTS to conditionally compile options.\nSo the idea is that CONFIG_xxx defines what signals are required, and then the code will flag a missing signal if it doesn\u0027t exist in DTS.",
